his and other recordings, visit the Miller Center's <a href=\"http://www.millercenter.virginia.edu/scripps/index.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">Scripps Library</a>.","source":"Franklin D. Roosevelt Presidential Library","taper":"White House","subject":"Franklin D. Roosevelt","publisher":"White House","numeric_id":"5136","boxid":"OL100020209","backup_location":"ia903600_5"},"reviews":[{"review_id":"21131","reviewbody":"This is a good demonstration as to how things have changed since 1940. This press conference was in the Oval Office...it was almost informal at times. FDR makes off handed comments that wouldn't be allowed today. it's obvious that he's \"off the cuff\". Nothing is written down. Just a different era.","reviewtitle":"Very interesting stuff","reviewer":"Mike Lindeen","reviewdate":"2004-09-18 12:28:24","createdate":"2004-09-18 12:28:24","stars":"5"},{"review_id":"37834","reviewbody":"Not a bad recording, they talk about Japan and housing for the GI (FDR has trouble with the word 'kitchenette' and he takes reporters mumbling questions. What's interesting about these conferences as well, is how short they are. 10 mins max!! Then they are shuffled off..","reviewtitle":"OK, bring em in...","reviewer":"Spuzz","reviewdate":"2005-04-07 13:20:08","createdate":"2005-04-07 13:20:08","stars":"2"}],"server":"ia801306.us.archive.org","uniq":535783,"workable_servers":["ia801306.us.archive.org","ia601306.us.archive.org"]}